  "finalText": "I've cancelled the wireless mouse on Marcus Ade's order O-2003 and refunded £73.50 to his card. The rest of the order is unchanged and will ship as planned.\n\n- **Checked first:** Right before making changes, I re-read the order. The mouse line (L1, 2 units) still hadn't shipped and hadn't been refunded, so this counts as a cancellation, not a return.\n- **Cancelled:** Only the mouse line was cancelled. The order is still pending.\n- **Refunded:** Refund RF-1 sent 7,350¢ (£73.50) to his card. That's the amount he actually paid for the line after the MOUSE25 discount, not the 9,800¢ list price (2 × 4,900¢).\n- **Restocked:** Cancelling didn't put any stock back, so I returned the 2 mice to stock separately. Wireless Mouse stock went from 30 to 32.\n- **Final check:** The mouse line is cancelled with 7,350¢ refunded to card. The order's total refunded is 7,350¢ of 19,950¢. The other two items, P-HUB (1 unit) and P-CAB (3 units), are still pending, and the shipping address hasn't changed.\n\nI didn't touch his other order (O-2001) or any other product. The order record shows \"today\" as 2026-07-25 while the system date is 2026-10-06. That doesn't matter here, because the return window only applies to returns, not cancellations.",
